lume>:<fpage>47724</fpage>&#x02013;47731.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12361956</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Leveen, P., M. Pekny, S. Gebre-Medhin, B. Swolin, E. Larsson, and C. Betsholtz. <year>1994</year>. Mice deficient for PDGF B show renal, cardiovascular, and hematological abnormalities. <source>Genes Dev.</source> <volume>8</volume>:<fpage>1875</fpage>&#x02013;1887.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7958863</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Li, C., M.B. Tropak, R. Gerlai, S. Clapoff, W. Abramow-Newerly, B. Trapp, A. Peterson, and J. Roder. <year>1994</year>. Myelination in the absence of myelin-associated glycoprotein. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>369</volume>:<fpage>747</fpage>&#x02013;750.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7516497</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Lindahl, P., B.R. Johansson, P. Leveen, and C. Betsholtz. <year>1997</year>. Pericyte loss and microaneurysm formation in PDGF-B-deficient mice. <source>Science.</source> <volume>277</volume>:<fpage>242</fpage>&#x02013;245.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9211853</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Liu, Y., R. Wada, T. Yamashita, Y. Mi, C.X. Deng, J.P. Hobson, H.M. Rosenfeldt, V.E. Nava, S.S. Chae, M.J. Lee, et al. <year>2000</year>. Edg-1, the G protein-coupled receptor for sphingosine-1-phosphate, is essential for vascular maturation. <source>J. Clin. Invest.</source> <volume>106</volume>:<fpage>951</fpage>&#x02013;961.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11032855</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Lowe, J.B., and J.D. Marth. <year>2003</year>. A genetic approach to mammalian glycan function. <source>Annu. Rev. Biochem.</source> <volume>72</volume>:<fpage>643</fpage>&#x02013;691.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12676797</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Mandel, U., O.W. Petersen, H. Sorensen, P. Vedtofte, S. Hakomori, H. Clausen, and E. Dabelsteen. <year>1991</year>. Simple mucin-type carbohydrates in oral stratified squamous and salivary gland epithelia. <source>J. Invest. Dermatol.</source> <volume>97</volume>:<fpage>713</fpage>&#x02013;721.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1940443</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">McCarty, J.H., R.A. Monahan-Earley, L.F. Brown, M. Keller, H. Gerhardt, K. Rubin, M. Shani, H.F. Dvorak, H. Wolburg, B.L. Bader, et al. <year>2002</year>. Defective associations between blood vessels and brain parenchyma lead to cerebral hemorrhage in mice lacking alphav integrins. <source>Mol. Cell. Biol.</source> <volume>22</volume>:<fpage>7667</fpage>&#x02013;7677.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12370313</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">McEver, R.P. <year>2002</year>. Selectins: lectins that initiate cell adhesion under flow. <source>Curr. Opin. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>14</volume>:<fpage>581</fpage>&#x02013;586.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12231353</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><citation citation-type="journal">Merry, A.H., R.J. Gilbert, D.A. Shore, L. Royle, O. Miroshnychenko, M. Vuong, M.R. Wormald, D.J. Harvey, R.A. Dwek, B.J. Classon, et al. <year>2003</year>. O-glycan sialylation and the structure of the stalk-like region of the T cell co-receptor CD8. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>278</volume>:<fpage>27119</fpage>&#x02013;27128.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12676960</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><citation citation-type="journal">Moody, A.M., D. Chui, P.A. Reche, J.J. Priatel, J.D. Marth, and E.L. Reinherz. <year>2001</year>. Developmentally regulated glycosylation of the CD8alphabeta coreceptor stalk modulates ligand binding. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>107</volume>:<fpage>501</fpage>&#x02013;512.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11719190</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><citation citation-type="journal">Moody, A.M., S.J. N